    "category": "Agave",
    "image_url": "/redesign/fig-blog-3.png",
    "body_text": "Mezcal is a Mexican agave spirit with a wide range of flavours. For NYC drinkers exploring it for the first time, the most useful question is often which mezcal is in the glass, rather than whether mezcal always tastes one particular way.\n\nLook at the label\n\nThe producer, origin and agave variety help describe a bottle's identity. Mezcal has regulated production requirements, and different producers can take different approaches within those rules. More detail about the bottle gives you a better starting point than a single adjective.\n\nNotice more than smoke\n\nRoasted agave can contribute distinctive character, but mezcal can also suggest fruit, herbs, earth and spice. Pay attention to aroma and texture as well as flavour. A gentler or less smoky profile is not automatically less interesting.\n\nIn a cocktail\n\nCitrus, bitters, fruit and herbs can each frame mezcal differently. Ask whether the drink is tart, sweet, bitter or spirit-led. The amount and type of mezcal matter, especially when it shares the recipe with another spirit.\n\nExplore the NYC drinks menus\n\nSilent H and Aitch's menu previews include agave-led drinks alongside other options. Browse the actual ingredients rather than assuming every mezcal style is offered. Both venues are opening soon, with service and reservation information to follow.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
    "id": "54403c84-eadb-4234-81d6-2aa6a0f5d2d6",
    "status": "published",
    "author_name": "Silent H NYC",
    "published_at": "2026-07-22T00:41:47.863445+00:00",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-07T12:00:00-04:00",
    "href": "/blogs/what-is-mezcal"
