    "category": "NYC",
    "image_url": "/redesign/fig-blog-1.png",
    "body_text": "Finding a favourite NYC spot can be more rewarding than chasing a secret address. Give yourself room to notice a small shop, a quiet street or a menu that catches your interest while keeping the day's practical details in view.\n\nExplore one neighbourhood at a time\n\nA focused walk leaves more room to pause than a route that crosses the city repeatedly. Manhattan's west side offers established places such as Chelsea Market alongside the streets around the Meatpacking District. Use the neighbourhood as a starting point rather than a checklist.\n\nCheck what is actually open\n\nA recommendation can outlive a venue's schedule or business. Confirm visitor information, booking requirements and the correct address before setting out. If a place has an unusual entrance or access arrangement, ask about it directly.\n\nLet the menu lead\n\nA restaurant or bar can become a personal favourite because of one dish or a thoughtful drink. Read descriptions and ask questions rather than assuming a place labelled hidden will suit everyone. Leave enough time to enjoy the stop you choose.\n\nFollow our NYC opening\n\nSilent H and Aitch are upcoming venues on West 13th Street. Explore the menu previews and opening updates without expecting a secret entrance, announced private room or available reservation. Those details are coming soon.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
