    "title": "Late-Night Food in NYC: Plan Before You Go",
    "category": "NYC",
    "image_url": "/menu/TACOLIV.webp",
    "body_text": "A late-night meal in New York depends on what the kitchen is serving when you arrive. A venue's closing time and its last food order can be different, so confirm the details before making the journey.\n\nCheck the kitchen separately\n\nLook for current kitchen hours, last orders and any shorter late-night menu. If the information is unclear, ask the venue directly. A bar remaining open does not guarantee that the full dinner menu is still available.\n\nChoose for the group\n\nDecide whether you want a quick bite or a seated meal. Check ingredients, portion sizes and non-alcoholic drinks alongside the food. People coming from a show or an event may arrive at different times, so share a clear meeting point.\n\nPlan the journey home\n\nCheck transit service and the route for your actual travel time. Leave room for weather, crowds and any changes to the evening. Keeping the dinner and next stop close together can make the plan easier.\n\nSilent H NYC service updates\n\nWe have not announced NYC late-night service or kitchen hours. Silent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street, with Aitch next door at 418. Browse the menus for a preview and check opening updates before planning a late-night visit.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
