    "slug": "nyc-nightlife",
    "title": "NYC After Dark: Plan a Meatpacking District Evening",
    "category": "NYC",
    "image_url": "/redesign/fig-blog-3.png",
    "body_text": "An NYC evening can be as simple as dinner and one well-chosen drinks stop. A clear route and current venue information leave more room to enjoy the night without rushing between neighbourhoods.\n\nAgree on the evening's pace\n\nSome groups want a long meal and conversation; others prefer a livelier setting. Decide before choosing venues. Check entry policies, accessibility and booking requirements directly rather than assuming one venue's arrangements apply to the next.\n\nUse the menus\n\nRead food and drinks lists before arriving. Think about whether everyone has options, including people choosing non-alcoholic drinks. If you plan dinner and a bar afterwards, allow enough time for both rather than stacking bookings too closely.\n\nKeep addresses and travel clear\n\nShare the exact meeting point and check transit for your travel date. A venue's neighbourhood description is helpful, but it does not replace its actual entrance address. Make the journey home part of the plan too.\n\nSilent H and Aitch are coming soon\n\nOur upcoming NYC restaurant and tequila bar will be neighbours on West 13th Street. Opening hours, programming and reservations have not been announced. Browse the menu previews and follow NYC updates before making either venue part of a confirmed night out.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
