    "category": "Experience",
    "image_url": "/redesign/fig-blog-1.png",
    "body_text": "A restaurant's design can help set the tone for an NYC evening, but a beautiful photograph is only one part of choosing a table. Consider the food, comfort and conversation alongside the look of the room.\n\nAsk what matters to your group\n\nLighting, seating and music affect how an evening feels. A setting that suits a celebration may not be ideal for a quiet catch-up. Check the practical details if you have particular access or seating needs rather than inferring them from a cropped image.\n\nLet the menu carry equal weight\n\nLook at ingredients, portions and drinks before deciding. A sharing menu can make the table feel sociable, while a simpler meal may fit a shorter visit. Tell the venue about dietary requirements early in the planning.\n\nUse current information\n\nA photographed space may look different during service or may belong to a different location. Confirm the venue and opening status before treating an image as a promise about the room you will enter.\n\nDiscover Silent H's NYC preview\n\nOur menu and story offer a starting point for the upcoming restaurant at 420 West 13th Street. We are opening soon. NYC event spaces and booking availability are coming soon too, so this guide does not promise a specific room or table arrangement.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
