    "category": "Events",
    "image_url": "/redesign/fig-blog-4.png",
    "body_text": "A birthday dinner in New York starts with the guest list and the kind of celebration you want. Set the practical details early so the evening can focus on the people around the table.\n\nChoose a comfortable group plan\n\nAgree on the date, approximate budget and whether guests will share plates or order individually. Include dietary requirements and accessibility needs. For a larger party, confirm the venue's group policy rather than assuming a regular table can accommodate everyone.\n\nAsk before adding extras\n\nCake, decorations, speeches and separate bills can have their own arrangements. Ask the venue what is possible and whether there are additional charges. Review deposits, cancellation terms and service charges before sending guests a final plan.\n\nKeep the invitation clear\n\nShare the confirmed address, arrival time and expectations around the meal. If you want drinks elsewhere afterwards, keep that route manageable and optional for guests who need to leave early.\n\nBirthdays at Silent H NYC\n\nOur restaurant is opening soon, and event planning is coming soon. We have not announced birthday packages, private spaces, group capacities or booking availability. Browse the current menu for future inspiration and look for updates on the Plan an Event page when arrangements are ready.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
