    "image_url": "/menu/TACOLIV.webp",
    "body_text": "A Yankees game can anchor a day in New York, but dinner plans need to fit the ballpark and your route. Yankee Stadium is in the Bronx, so a Manhattan meal should be treated as a separate stop with travel time built in.\n\nStart with the game information\n\nCheck the date, start time, entry instructions and current stadium policies through the Yankees' official information. Allow room for crowds and the journey to your entrance. A ticketed event is easier to enjoy when the meal does not end at the last possible moment.\n\nDecide where dinner belongs\n\nEating near the ballpark and dining elsewhere in the city are different plans. Choose based on the time available and how much travelling you want to do. Check the restaurant's opening information and kitchen timing for your date.\n\nA Meatpacking District meal\n\nSilent H's upcoming address is 420 West 13th Street in Manhattan. It is not next to Yankee Stadium, and we are not advertising a game-day shuttle, special menu or quick transfer time. Plan the actual journey separately.\n\nWait for opening details\n\nSilent H NYC is opening soon, with reservations and operating information coming soon. Browse our food menu for future plans, then confirm opening and service details before including us in a game-day itinerary.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
