    "slug": "corporate-event-planning-nyc",
    "title": "Planning a Corporate Dinner or Event in NYC",
    "category": "Events",
    "image_url": "/redesign/fig-blog-4.png",
    "body_text": "An NYC corporate gathering needs a venue brief that is clear about purpose as well as headcount. A team dinner, client reception and presentation can require different seating, timing and service arrangements.\n\nWrite the brief first\n\nInclude the date, guest count, budget, format and expected duration. Note accessibility and dietary requirements, along with any need for microphones, screens or a quiet area for speeches. These details help a venue say what it can actually support.\n\nConfirm the proposed arrangement\n\nAsk for the available layout and its real capacity rather than relying on a general venue list. Clarify privacy, arrival arrangements, food and beverage service and any technical support. Get the inclusions and costs in writing before committing.\n\nPlan for the guests\n\nChoose a location that fits where people are travelling from, then share the confirmed address and schedule. Allow time for arrivals and avoid letting a tightly timed transfer determine the whole event.\n\nEvent planning at Silent H NYC\n\nOur Plan an Event page is coming soon. NYC event rooms, capacities, packages and corporate booking availability have not been announced. This article is a general planning guide, not a list of spaces we currently offer. We will share event details when ready.\n\nSilent H NYC opening updates\n\nSilent H is opening soon at 420 West 13th Street in the Meatpacking District. Aitch will be next door at 418 West 13th Street. Reservations are coming soon. Follow our NYC opening updates before planning a visit.",
